<title>UK: Weather closes Novorossiisk over weekend - shipper.</title>
<headline>Weather closes Novorossiisk over weekend - shipper.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-09-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Berthing at Russia's main oil export terminal in the Black Sea, Novorossiisk, resumed at 0845 local time on Monday, having been suspended at 1300 on Friday due to bad weather, a shipping inspector said.</p>
<p>Operations were also suspended on Thursday evening last week, but reopened for two and a half hours before closing again on Friday.</p>
<p>Oil traders said the closures would exacerbate the existing five- to six-day delay in September loadings of Urals crude from the port.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 8145</p>
</text>
